# xmonad projects: copy to ~/.config/xmonad/projects (that file is not in the
# repo) and adjust. One project per line:
#   name | directory | command; command
# super+shift+p: jump to a project (its workspace is created when needed and,
# while empty, the commands start). Terminals started on a project's workspace
# open in its directory. super+ctrl+p sends the focused window to a project.
# A digit as the name gives that numbered workspace a directory.
#
# work  | ~/dev/src       | wezterm; librewolf https://gitlab.example.com/dashboard/merge_requests
# dots  | ~/dots-debian   | wezterm
# notes | ~/notes         | wezterm start -- nvim .
# 2     | ~/dev/src       |
